===============================================================================
§3  DECLARED DEPENDENCIES — the Rust wrapper only
===============================================================================

`rust/` is a safe wrapper over the C ABI: `insimul-sys` (raw FFI, **no
dependencies at all** — the ABI is a handful of functions over `*const c_char`)
and `insimul` (the idiomatic API). Two direct dependencies, `serde` and
`serde_json`, which pull in nine more. That is the entire external surface of
this repository, and the reason `scripts/check-open-boundary.mjs` can claim the
dependency graph is *closed* rather than merely deny-listed
(`docs/pre-open-audit.md` §2.3).

**None of this is redistributed by this repository.** A C, C++, GDScript or
browser consumer of `libinsimul` resolves none of it; a Rust consumer resolves
it themselves, from crates.io, under these crates' own terms. Nine of the eleven
are build-time only (proc macros and their support crates), reached only when
`serde_derive` runs. Every version below is the one `rust/Cargo.lock` resolves,
and `scripts/check-attribution.mjs` fails if that stops being true — because a
lock bump re-opens the license question, which is the only reason to record a
version at all.

A note on the copyright lines: most of these crates' `LICENSE-MIT` files carry
**no copyright notice at all** — they are the bare permission text. Where that
is so, the `Copyright` field names the crate's declared authors and says which
it is. Inventing a notice for a file that has none would be a fabrication in a
document whose entire value is that it is not one.

